      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, that's much better. i appreciate you cutting out the extra stuff. \n\none thing i've been seeing in my shop is that some of these turbo units make this really loud, high-pitched whistling or even a screaming sound when they're spooling up, especially on the older models. is that whistle just a normal part of the air rushing through the blades at those speeds, or is there a specific reason why it sounds so... well, intense? like, is it just the physics of the air, or is there something mechanical causing that specific pitch? \n\ni want to make sure i can explain the difference between a normal sound and a mechanical issue on my exam.",
      "source": "evaluator"
